      "writtenOn": "2026-11-18T11:52:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I looked at it, but it doesn\u0027t fit, for the reason you mention. Graceful stop answers \u0027should shutdown wait for this?\u0027, and it is enabled by read and write commands alike: query, ls-projects, show-queue and version as well as review, create-project, create-branch and git upload/receive-pack. So it can\u0027t tell which commands are safe to drop. It is also a sticky flag on the SshSession, set from inside run(), while destroy() has to decide per command and possibly before run() has started. A query should be waited for on shutdown but cancelled on disconnect, so the two need separate flags. That\u0027s why I kept cancelOnClientDisconnect().",
      "parentUuid": "3f5b44f4_813a4bb6",
      "revId": "35fdf2c04762406d4a1cd9e2ed91c74d9e3cc4cf",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
