      "writtenOn": "2026-11-18T11:52:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Good question, I\u0027ve made the message explicit. Neither this change nor I8155a9e56f touches git upload/receive-pack or stream-events. They aren\u0027t SshCommands, so on disconnect BaseCommand#destroy still interrupts their thread as it always did. For pushes there is a second, older mechanism: ReceiveCommits uses the MultiProgressMonitor as a RequestStateProvider, which reports CLIENT_CLOSED_REQUEST once sending progress to the client fails, and the remaining commands are then rejected. So yes, a push can be cut short too. But that logic lives in ReceiveCommits, is shared with HTTP pushes, and needs a different fix than the SSH opt-in.",
